VERDICT: REJECTED
The redesign is largely implemented, but it introduces a clear functional regression in primary navigation, so this should not be marked complete yet.

Critical findings / analysis:
- **Broken main navigation anchors**: Header and mobile menu still link to `#program` (lines ~921, 945), but that section ID no longer exists after the redesign. The section is now `#program-unggulan` (line ~1086). This breaks a core user flow (top-level nav to Program section).
- The rest of sections 7–13 appear present and wired (`#mengapa-sci`, `#testimonials`, `#galeri`, `#tutor`, `#bantuan`, `#cabang`, and 4-column footer), so scope coverage is mostly there.
- Minor non-blocking quality issue observed: footer contact line has `font-size:.82px` typo (likely meant `.82rem`), causing near-invisible text.

Security:
- None observed (no serious authz/injection/secrets exposure issues in this diff).

Next actions:
1. Update all remaining `href="#program"` links (desktop + mobile nav and any other occurrences) to `href="#program-unggulan"` or add a compatible `id="program"` alias section.
2. Re-run a quick anchor audit (`rg 'href="#'`) to ensure every in-page link targets an existing section ID.
3. Fix the footer font-size typo (`.82px` -> `.82rem`) before final handoff.

